{"_v":4,"id":"a-christmas-carol-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":76.01,"rc":10,"bd":{"rave":4,"positive":5,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Aliya Al-Hassan","o":"London Theatre","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":2,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/a-christmas-carol-review-old-vic-2026","d":"2026-11-25","q":"From the mince pies and satsumas given out as you enter, to the impossibly jaunty cast and falling snow, this is a Christmas production that still warms you to your core.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Rachel Halliburton","o":"The Arts Desk","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://theartsdesk.com/theatre/christmas-carol-old-vic-review-giles-terera-sensational-scrooge-rolls-royce-christmas-show","d":"2026-11-25","q":"Terera is a sensational Scrooge, swinging from uncompromising severity in the early scenes to joy of such giddiness that it makes you want to dance in the aisles.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":2,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/a-christmas-carol-the-old-vic-review","d":"2026-11-25","q":"A CHRISTMAS CAROL is charm itself, runs 2 hours and 20 mins (including interval), and continues until 9th January 2027.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Franco Milazzo","o":"BroadwayWorld","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":2,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.broadwayworld.com/westend/article/Review-A-CHRISTMAS-CAROL-Old-Vic-20261124","d":"2026-11-24","q":"Jack Thorne's script is pitched so an eight-year-old can follow it, then slips in things the parents will recognise, and the children only will later: deep regret, the lifelong impact of bad parenting, love postponed until it has gone, and how quickly a life folds itself away.","or":"4/5 stars"},{"cn":"Rebecca Clifton","o":"British Theatre Guide","s":65,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"v":"mixed","u":"https://www.britishtheatreguide.info/reviews/a-christmas-car-the-old-vic-the-26237","d":"2026-11-25","q":"This production is missing hues and shadows of previous ones."},{"cn":"Miriam Sallon","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":57,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"v":"positive","u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/a-christmas-carol-with-giles-terera-at-the-old-vic-review_1738234/","d":"2026-11-25","q":"Thorne and Warchus do a beautiful job of bringing a crotchety London crowd together, with much Christmas cheer for adults and children alike, and a hot mince pie to boot.","or":"3/5 stars"},{"cn":"Alexandra Tullah","o":"West End Best Friend","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"v":"rave","u":"https://www.westendbestfriend.co.uk/news/review-a-christmas-carol-old-vic-theatre-nov-2026","d":"2026-11-25","q":"The Old Vic's A Christmas Carol remains a lovely festive treat that can warm even the coldest of hearts."},{"cn":"Giles Broadbent","o":"The Spy in the Stalls","s":97,"b":"Rave","t":4,"v":"rave","u":"https://thespyinthestalls.com/2026/11/a-christmas-carol-9/","d":"2026-11-25","q":"It is the greatest Christmas story ever told."},{"cn":"Hay Brunsdon","o":"London Theatre Direct","s":94,"b":"Rave","t":4,"v":"rave","u":"https://www.londontheatredirect.com/news/a-christmas-carol-at-the-old-vic-review-a-festive-feast-of-dickensian-magic","d":"2026-11-25","q":"Ten years on, this production still has plenty of festive magic to share.","or":"4.5/5 stars"},{"cn":null,"o":"London Unattached","s":92,"b":"Rave","t":4,"v":"rave","u":"https://www.london-unattached.com/a-christmas-carol-the-old-vic-theatre/","d":"2026-11-25","q":"Matthew Warchus's richly atmospheric production has lost none of its magic."}],"au":{"score":93.66,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"sp":{"s":95,"c":220,"sr":4.76},"lb":{"s":94,"c":37,"sr":4.7},"ltd":{"s":98,"c":815,"sr":4.9},"mz":{"s":86,"c":501,"sr":4.3}}},"cn":{"t":"The Old Vic's A Christmas Carol, now in its 10th season, remains a beloved festive institution. Critics largely praise its emotional power and Jack Thorne's adaptation, though a few find the familiar formula showing its age.","rc":10},"sh":{"wk":"20270104","days":[{"m